    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_f01194c7",
      "@type": "SemioticProjection",
      "instance_name": "semiotic_projection_1",
      "label": "User projected onto Yoda as 'the stupid'",
      "description": "The user is projected onto the visual material of Yoda, who is being used as a stand-in for 'the stupid' as defined by the overlaid text. The meme's structure implies that the viewer (user) is the target of the ridicule, with Yoda serving as a visual proxy for the user's perceived stupidity. This projection is implicit, not explicit, but is inferred from the meme's ironic framing and the common meme convention of self-referential humor where the viewer identifies with the subject of the mockery.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
